Task: Enrich order-service/inventory-service logging (Phase 1, tasks 1-7 combined)

Summary: Added log4cats-testing (Test-scoped) to both services' own build.sbt
entries. Wrote failing tests (StructuredTestingLogger) for request-received/
completed logging on all endpoints (incl. GET /orders/{id}'s 404 path),
error-path logging around inventory.reserve/store.create in order-service,
and the induced-failure trigger's warn log in inventory-service — confirmed
each Red, then implemented to Green. Dropped an initially-added onError wrap
around InventoryStore.reserve (an unconditional in-memory write that can't
fail — would have been dead, uncoverable code) per "don't add error handling
for scenarios that can't happen." Added startup config-summary logging to
both Main.scala's, verified manually via console output (bgRun + curl).
Full suite green (purerest/orderService/inventoryService), 100% coverage on
OrderRoutes.scala/InventoryRoutes.scala, scalafmt clean on touched files.

Files changed: build.sbt, modules/order-service/src/main/scala/orderservice/
{Main,OrderRoutes}.scala, modules/order-service/src/test/scala/orderservice/
OrderRoutesSuite.scala, modules/inventory-service/src/main/scala/
inventoryservice/{Main,InventoryRoutes}.scala, modules/inventory-service/
src/test/scala/inventoryservice/InventoryRoutesSuite.scala

Why: Current logging was thin (2 lines total, no error-path or
